{"id":"rickshaw-run","title":"Rickshaw Run: Kochi to Jaisalmer","who":"The Adventurists · since 2006","when":"Three times a year (January, April, August–September)","vehicle":"A 7-horsepower auto-rickshaw","kind":"rally","color":"#16a34a","summary":"Teams drive three-wheeled auto-rickshaws across India, about 2,800–3,500 km in two weeks, with no set route and no support, raising money for charity. Recent editions run between Fort Kochi in Kerala and Jaisalmer in the Thar Desert, alternating direction; earlier ones went to Shillong, Darjeeling, Gangtok or Kathmandu and Pokhara in Nepal.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Rickshaw Run","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rickshaw_Run"},{"label":"The Adventurists: Rickshaw Run India","url":"https://www.theadventurists.com/?p=2431"},{"label":"Scroll.in: 2,764 km from Cochin to Jaisalmer by auto-rickshaw","url":"https://scroll.in/video/861469/scroll_in"}],"approximate":"One common route up the west coast and through Rajasthan; every team picks its own way.","km":2648,"bbox":[70.7599,9.9675,76.2422,27.0978],"stops":[{"name":"Fort Kochi","place":"Fort Kochi, Kerala","at":[9.9676,76.2422],"text":"The start among Chinese fishing nets, after a day learning to drive a rickshaw.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Kochi%2C_Fishing_nets_at_sunset%2C_Kerala%2C_India.jpg/500px-Kochi%2C_Fishing_nets_at_sunset%2C_Kerala%2C_India.jpg","page":"Fort Kochi","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kochi%2C_Fishing_nets_at_sunset%2C_Kerala%2C_India.jpg","credit":"Vyacheslav Argenberg","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Mangalore","place":"Mangalore, India","at":[12.8698,74.843],"text":"North up the Malabar coast.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Growing_skylines_of_the_Mangalore_CBD_region.jpg/500px-Growing_skylines_of_the_Mangalore_CBD_region.jpg","page":"Mangaluru","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Growing_skylines_of_the_Mangalore_CB